KZ3 patch 2161 (RSX pass 149): sampler cache hash index (RSX_SMP_INDEX) and finer texture-loop timers (RSX_PERF_DRAW).
1. sampler_slot() scanned every cached sampler key (up to 128 x 16-byte memcmp) for each enabled texture unit that missed the
   binding row. rsx_smp_index.h keeps an open-addressed index (uint16, 512 entries, <= 25 % load, no deletion) beside g.smp_keys;
   keys are unique, so a hit returns the same slot as the scan. RSX_SMP_INDEX unset or 0 = the scan (default since pass 151), 1 = index, "verify" = index plus scan with a
   logged disagreement ([smp-index] verify FAILED). Host test tools/smoke/test_smp_index.sh: index == scan over
   720,000 random lookups, negative control (an index missing one add is caught), micro-benchmark: scan 7.8/12.3/20.0/32.7 ns per
   lookup at 16/32/64/128 cached keys, index 2.2-2.4 ns. The saving per draw is bounded by (enabled units that miss the row) x
   that difference, i.e. well under 1 us of a ~20 us draw; it is a small win, not the texture-loop lever.
2. RSX_PERF_DRAW=1 gains three rows under "texture loop (minus binds)": "loop: row check (all units)" (rsx_tex_l1_hit on every
   unit), "loop: register decode (row miss)" (ld_tex_get) and "loop: sampler key+slot". The rest of the loop is the remainder.

